herolte: a first CPU governor for the Mongoose cluster, herogov=1 (0434)

E-0286 (min58-min60): with the screen on and the CPU all but idle (all 13-31 % of 800 %) the phone draws ~850 mA at 1976-2288 MHz and ~480 mA at the bootloader's 728 MHz / 675 mV; under load (Safari) 1.9-2.6 A. The idle cores leak at the raised voltage. herogov=1: the power thread measures the busy fraction of cores 4-7 every 200 ms (recount idle time; herolte_cluster_busy_mach in osfmk/kern/processor.c) and keeps the cluster at herocpu_mhz only while it is above 15 %; after 1 s below 6 % it goes to the bootloader numbers (hc_go_low), the same transition the screen-off and heat logic already use. Off unless herogov=1, which also sets the 5 s battery poll (the boot line has no room for another argument).

